2. Workflow
    TrajectoryBuilder
            │
            ▼
    Build DriveTrajectory
            │
            ▼
    TrajectoryPlanner
            │
            ▼
    CompositeDrivePath
            │
            ▼
    TrajectoryProfile
            │
            ▼
    DriveMotionController
            │
            ▼
            Robot

    Notes:
    Each class has a single responsibility:
    - DrivePath: "Where should the robot travel?"
    - TrajectoryBuilder: "How do I assemble a complete trajectory?"
    - TrajectoryPlanner: "How fast should the robot travel at each point?"
    - TrajectoryProfile: "Where should the robot be at time t?"
    - DriveMotionController: "How do I make the robot follow that trajectory?"

    DriveTrajectory would internally contain:

    CompositeDrivePath
    TrajectoryProfile
    final target pose
    total distance
    total time
    waypoint list
    motion constraints

    This keeps DriveMotionController simple and makes the API much cleaner as your framework grows.
    I think this will make the library easier to maintain and much easier for your FTC students to understand.

    DriveTrajectory the central object that represents everything needed for autonomous or semi-autonomous motion.

    DriveTrajectory would internally contain:

        CompositeDrivePath
        TrajectoryProfile
        final target pose
        total distance
        total time
        waypoint list
        motion constraints